# Environment Variables Template
#
# Choose the section that matches your build tool and copy the variables
# into the correct file.  Never commit that file to version control.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRA (create-react-app / react-scripts)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Active env file priority: .env.local > .env.development.local > .env
# Only variables prefixed REACT_APP_ are embedded in the browser bundle.
# The dev server MUST be restarted after any change to .env.local.
#
# Copy to: .env.local   (CRA loads this automatically; add it to .gitignore)
#
# ⚠️  PLACEHOLDER TRAP: if you copy .env.example without replacing the values,
#     CRA will embed the literal placeholder strings ("your-api-token-here").
#     The Instana API will return 401 Unauthorized.  Always verify the file
#     contains real values: grep "your-" .env.local should produce no output.
#
REACT_APP_INSTANA_URL=https://myunit.instana.io
REACT_APP_INSTANA_TOKEN=
REACT_APP_APPLICATION_ID=
REACT_APP_TIME_WINDOW_MS=86400000
REACT_APP_GRANULARITY_SEC=3600
REACT_APP_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS=60000

# CRA proxy — add to package.json (not .env) to avoid CORS during development:
# "proxy": "https://myunit.instana.io"
# This forwards every /api/* request from the dev server to Instana, so the
# browser never makes a cross-origin request directly.  Restart the dev server
# after changing the proxy value.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vite
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Active env file priority: .env.local > .env.development > .env
# Only variables prefixed VITE_ are embedded in the browser bundle.
# The dev server MUST be restarted after any change to .env.local.
#
# Copy to: .env.local   (Vite loads this automatically; add it to .gitignore)
#
VITE_INSTANA_BASE_URL=https://myunit.instana.io
VITE_INSTANA_API_TOKEN=
VITE_INSTANA_APPLICATION_ID=
VITE_INSTANA_TIME_WINDOW_MS=86400000
VITE_INSTANA_GRANULARITY_SEC=3600
VITE_INSTANA_REFRESH_INTERVAL_MS=60000

# Vite proxy — add to vite.config.ts (not .env):
# server: { proxy: { '/api': { target: 'https://myunit.instana.io', changeOrigin: true, secure: false } } }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node.js scripts / backend
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to: .env   (loaded by dotenv; add it to .gitignore)
#
INSTANA_BASE_URL=https://myunit.instana.io
INSTANA_API_TOKEN=
INSTANA_APPLICATION_ID=
INSTANA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
INSTANA_MAX_RETRIES=3

---

## Authentication

Instana uses a custom auth header — **not** Basic auth or Bearer:

```
Authorization: apiToken <your-token>
```

Using `Authorization: Basic ...` returns **401 Unauthorized**.  
Using a placeholder token returns **401 Unauthorized**.

---

## Security Reminders

1. Add `.env.local` / `.env` to `.gitignore` immediately after creating it.
2. Use a **read-only** API token for monitoring integrations — never an admin token.
3. Rotate the token if it is ever accidentally exposed (committed to git, logged, etc.).
4. In CI/CD, inject the token as a masked secret — never hard-code it.
5. For production React apps, **do not** embed the token in the browser bundle.
   Route API calls through a backend proxy that injects the token server-side.

---

## Common 401 Causes

| Cause | Fix |
|---|---|
| `.env.local` was never created — only `.env.example` exists | Copy `.env.example` → `.env.local` and replace all placeholders |
| `.env.local` was created but placeholders not replaced | Edit `.env.local`; replace `your-api-token-here` etc. with real values |
| Dev server not restarted after editing `.env.local` | Stop the server (`Ctrl+C`), then `npm start` again |
| Wrong auth header format (`Bearer` or `Basic`) | Use `Authorization: apiToken <token>` |
| Token missing `canConfigureApplications` permission | Regenerate token with the correct permissions in the Instana UI |
